[I] A statically typed compiled systems programming language

[T] Nim is a statically typed compiled systems programming language. It
[T] combines successful concepts from mature languages like Python, Ada
[T] and Modula.

[U] https://nim-lang.org

[A] Andreas Rumpf
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/development
[R] + arm arm64 hppa loongarch64 mips mips64 powerpc powerpc64 riscv64 s390x sparc sparc64 x86 x86-64

[L] MIT
[V] 2.4.0

[D] 381554afede644841406b2ca999fcbd9f7ce7010f9d611f8ef8db70e nim-2.4.0.tar.xz https://nim-lang.org/download/

# TODO: make it honor $prefix
[ $prefix_auto = 1 ] && prefix=opt/nim && set_confopt
hook_add postmake 5 "./install $root/${prefix%/*}"
